IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ccc-core`

-- ccc19-s492-26.l4 -- Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46, s 492.26 Case Complexity (text lines 10985-10997), in PART XV.1 Unreasonable Delay.
-- LAYER 1: the law, objectively, from the text alone. Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website
-- consolidation (current to 2026-09-30); not the official text, and nothing here is claimed verified against the official text.
-- Both subsections are duties of the court ("shall consider"). Each is encoded as a decision function (MAYBE BOOLEAN) and as a regulative rule (DEONTIC).
-- A failed "In determining" or "If" gate of a duty is JUST FALSE (rule of 2026-10-29 (a); NOTES.md, Marginal readings); a list the text does not close is NOTHING.

§ `s 492.26(1) -- the court shall consider whether there are any relevant factors that contributed or will contribute to making the case complex`

-- "In determining whether there has been or will be unreasonable delay, the court shall consider whether there are any relevant factors that contributed or will contribute to making the case complex."
-- The duty lies on the court while it is determining whether there has been or will be unreasonable delay; outside that determination the subsection says nothing is owed (JUST FALSE).
-- src:10987 | 492.26 (1) In determining whether there has been or will be unreasonable delay, the court shall consider whether there are any relevant factors that contributed or will contribute to making the case complex.
@ref Criminal Code s 492.26(1) (src:10987)
GIVEN `the court is determining whether there has been or will be unreasonable delay` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 492.26(1) the court must consider whether any relevant factors contributed or will contribute to making the case complex` MEANS
    IF `the court is determining whether there has been or will be unreasonable delay`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In determining whether there has been or will be unreasonable delay"

@ref Criminal Code s 492.26(1) (src:10987)
DECLARE `s 492.26(1) act` IS ONE OF
    `s 492.26(1) consider whether there are any relevant factors that contributed or will contribute to making the case complex`

@ref Criminal Code s 492.26(1) (src:10987)
GIVEN `the court is determining whether there has been or will be unreasonable delay` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 492.26(1) act`
`s 492.26(1) the duty of the court to consider case complexity` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 492.26(1) the court must consider whether any relevant factors contributed or will contribute to making the case complex` `the court is determining whether there has been or will be unreasonable delay`
    WHEN JUST owed THEN
        IF owed
        THEN PARTY `the court`
             MUST `s 492.26(1) consider whether there are any relevant factors that contributed or will contribute to making the case complex`
             HENCE FULFILLED
             LEST BREACH BY `the court` BECAUSE "s 492.26(1): the court did not consider whether any relevant factors contributed or will contribute to making the case complex"
        ELSE FULFILLED
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FULFILLED

§ `s 492.26(2) -- applications and motions: the factors the court shall also consider`

-- "If the case involved or will involve applications or motions, either before, during or after the trial, the court shall also consider the following factors in assessing whether the case is complex:"
-- followed by paragraphs (a) to (h). Paragraphs (a) to (g) name seven factors; paragraph (h) is "any factor that the court finds relevant in assessing the complexity of the applications or motions",
-- which hands the judgment to the court: it is a plain input (the court finds the factor relevant, or not). The list is not closed by "only", so a factor that is none of (a) to (h) is NOT COVERED (fork F5).
-- src:10989 | (2) If the case involved or will involve applications or motions, either before, during or after the trial, the court shall also consider the following factors in assessing whether the case is complex:
-- src:10990 | (a) the number of applications or motions;
-- src:10991 | (b) whether any of the applications or motions required or will require scheduling court dates separately and in advance of trial dates;
-- src:10992 | (c) whether any adjournments were or will be required in order to complete the steps required by any of the applications or motions;
-- src:10993 | (d) whether more than one judicial decision was or will be needed to complete the steps required by any of the applications or motions
-- src:10994 | (e) the amount of cumulative court time that was or will be required to adjudicate the applications or motions;
-- src:10995 | (f) the need for trial continuation dates arising from the applications or motions that required more time than anticipated;
-- src:10996 | (g) the need for trial continuation dates arising from the applications or motions that were not scheduled in advance of the trial; and
-- src:10997 | (h) any factor that the court finds relevant in assessing the complexity of the applications or motions.
@ref Criminal Code s 492.26(2)(a) to (h) (src:10989-10997)
DECLARE `s 492.26(2) factor` IS ONE OF
    `s 492.26(2)(a) the number of applications or motions`
    `s 492.26(2)(b) whether any of the applications or motions required or will require scheduling court dates separately and in advance of trial dates`
    `s 492.26(2)(c) whether any adjournments were or will be required in order to complete the steps required by any of the applications or motions`
    `s 492.26(2)(d) whether more than one judicial decision was or will be needed to complete the steps required by any of the applications or motions`
    `s 492.26(2)(e) the amount of cumulative court time that was or will be required to adjudicate the applications or motions`
    `s 492.26(2)(f) the need for trial continuation dates arising from the applications or motions that required more time than anticipated`
    `s 492.26(2)(g) the need for trial continuation dates arising from the applications or motions that were not scheduled in advance of the trial`
    `s 492.26(2)(h) another factor, not named in paragraphs (a) to (g)`

@ref Criminal Code s 492.26(2) (src:10989-10997)
GIVEN `the case involved or will involve applications or motions, either before, during or after the trial` IS A BOOLEAN
      factor IS A `s 492.26(2) factor`
      `the court finds the factor relevant in assessing the complexity of the applications or motions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 492.26(2) the court must also consider the factor in assessing whether the case is complex` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the case involved or will involve applications or motions, either before, during or after the trial`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the case involved or will involve applications or motions, either before, during or after the trial"
        IF factor EQUALS `s 492.26(2)(h) another factor, not named in paragraphs (a) to (g)` THEN
            IF `the court finds the factor relevant in assessing the complexity of the applications or motions`
            THEN JUST TRUE   -- (h): "any factor that the court finds relevant in assessing the complexity of the applications or motions"
            ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "the following factors"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE   -- (a) to (g): each is named in the list

@ref Criminal Code s 492.26(2) (src:10989-10997)
DECLARE `s 492.26(2) act` IS ONE OF
    `s 492.26(2) consider the factor in assessing whether the case is complex` HAS `the factor considered` IS A `s 492.26(2) factor`

@ref Criminal Code s 492.26(2) (src:10989-10997)
GIVEN `the case involved or will involve applications or motions, either before, during or after the trial` IS A BOOLEAN
      factor IS A `s 492.26(2) factor`
      `the court finds the factor relevant in assessing the complexity of the applications or motions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 492.26(2) act`
`s 492.26(2) the duty of the court to consider the factor` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 492.26(2) the court must also consider the factor in assessing whether the case is complex` `the case involved or will involve applications or motions, either before, during or after the trial` factor `the court finds the factor relevant in assessing the complexity of the applications or motions`
    WHEN JUST owed THEN
        IF owed
        THEN PARTY `the court`
             MUST `s 492.26(2) consider the factor in assessing whether the case is complex` considered PROVIDED considered EQUALS factor
             HENCE FULFILLED
             LEST BREACH BY `the court` BECAUSE "s 492.26(2): the court did not consider the factor in assessing whether the case is complex"
        ELSE FULFILLED
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FULFILLED
